# The road strips of the basic content set in all six directions: a loop from the castle's flag round the node 17,7. It needs no
# install and no SIEDLER_DIR. Run it with the seed and size of basic-production.play:
#   sh tools/play-run.sh basic-roads --game-view --content-set basic --seed 4455544685788642 --size 1 --fps 10
# On that map the castle stands at 15,5, its flag at 16,6. The loop goes east, south-east, south, west, north-west, and north
# (17,6 18,7 18,8 17,8 16,7) back to 16,6. The generated map gives those nodes the heights 15 (16,6), 13, 10, 11, 13, and 15 (16,7),
# so the strips, each drawn from the node it leaves east, south-east, or south, have the height differences 2 (16,6 east),
# 3 (17,6 south-east), -1 (18,7 south), 2 (17,8 east), 2 (16,7 south-east), and 0 (16,6 south): a gap at a node shows a strip
# that misses its end node.
expect seed = 4455544685788642
expect size = 1
wait 0.3
click-tile 15 5
wait 0.3
button Road
click-tile 16 6
click-tile 17 6
click-tile 18 7
click-tile 18 8
click-tile 17 8
click-tile 16 7
click-tile 16 6
button Road
wait 0.3
expect-count road = 6
shot loop 15 4 5 5
